      "derivation": "AppendFuture.Response explicitly requires Error to have returned and states that the response is valid only on success. This applies directly because pipelineDecode consumes AppendFuture through AppendPipeline.Consumer. The decoder calls Response without calling Error, then interprets Term and Success before updating replication progress. Consumer readiness is not documented as success. The concrete network pipeline calls future.respond(err) and delivers the future without filtering err; decodeResponse can decode a response and still return an RPC error. These observations justify checking the interface consumption relation independently of whether a harmful failed response is reachable from a built-in follower.",
